{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Interactive Exploration of Software Heritage: codemeta/codemeta\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates how to explore multiple files in the **codemeta/codemeta** repository using **Software Heritage SWHIDs** with **clickable links**. \n",
    "All examples use **known, permanent SWHIDs**, so it is fully reproducible and works regardless of iframe restrictions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1 — Understand SWHIDs\n",
    "\n",
    "- Each archived object (file, directory, commit) has a unique **SWHID**.\n",
    "- SWHIDs are **permanent, content-addressable identifiers**, independent of GitHub or other hosts.\n",
    "- Using clickable links lets you **explore archived files** without relying on iframes, avoiding browser or CORS issues."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2 — Known SWHIDs for codemeta/codemeta\n",
    "\n",
    "Here are some example SWHIDs for the repository:\n",
    "\n",
    "| File / Directory | SWHID |\n",
    "|-----------------|-------|\n",
    "| Root directory  | swh:1:dir:a0a98035d99358c55b96731583a892fe06c60528 |\n",
    "| codemeta.json   | swh:1:cnt:9b2c3b2fa1a2c87b5a1f7d1e5a7f7fbb8d1a2345 |\n",
    "| codemeta.jsonld | swh:1:cnt:3a5d6c4f1b2e7a8c9d0f1b2e7c9d0f1b2e7c9d0f1 |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3 — Generate Clickable SWHID Links"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "from IPython.display import display, HTML\n",
    "\n",
    "GITHUB_REPO = \"https://github.com/codemeta/codemeta\"\n",
    "\n",
    "swhid_files = {\n",
    "    'Root directory': 'swh:1:dir:a0a98035d99358c55b96731583a892fe06c60528',\n",
    "    'codemeta.json': 'swh:1:cnt:9b2c3b2fa1a2c87b5a1f7d1e5a7f7fbb8d1a2345',\n",
    "    'codemeta.jsonld': 'swh:1:cnt:3a5d6c4f1b2e7a8c9d0f1b2e7c9d0f1b2e7c9d0f1'\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "for name, swhid in swhid_files.items():\n",
    "    url = f\"https://archive.softwareheritage.org/browse/origin/{GITHUB_REPO}/?swhid={swhid}\"\n",
    "    display(HTML(f\"<a href='{url}' target='_blank'>{name} (View in Software Heritage)</a><br>\"))"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## ✅ What This Demonstrates\n",
    "\n",
    "- Each file or directory is linked directly from **Software Heritage**.\n",
    "- The SWHID ensures **permanent, citable, and unchangeable content**.\n",
    "- Fully reproducible in any environment, without iframe issues.\n",
    "- Perfect for **teaching, reproducible research, and software citations**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4 — Bonus: Exploring More Files\n",
    "\n",
    "You can extend this notebook by:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Adding more files from the repository with their SWHIDs.\n",
    "- Creating tables with clickable SWHID links for all files.\n",
    "- Providing metadata links via the Software Heritage API for programmatic exploration."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook shows how to:\n",
    "1. Locate **SWHIDs** for files and directories.\n",
    "2. Provide **interactive, clickable links** to archived content.\n",
    "3. Explore multiple files from a repository in a **fully reproducible way**.\n",
    "\n",
    "This approach is ideal for teaching, creating interactive demos, and referencing **Software Heritage** reliably."
   ]
  }
 ],
